2. Array Representation
I will use a two-dimensional array to represent parking floors and slots.
String[][] parking = new String[3][10];


- 3 rows represent 3 floors.
- 10 columns represent 10 slots on each floor.
- null indicates an available slot.
- A vehicle number indicates an occupied slot.
A 2D array is suitable because parking slots are arranged floor-wise.
3. Type Conversion and Casting
Type conversion is required when calculating parking fees. Integer division may produce incorrect results.

Example:
int minutes = 90;
double hours = minutes / 60;


Output: 1.0 (incorrect, because integer division removes the decimal part).

Correct method:
double hours = minutes / 60.0;
double fee = hours * 20;
System.out.println(fee);


Output: 30.0

Using 60.0 ensures floating-point division and avoids precision loss.
